\tag{fdip}
\title{The index for scalar fields in disjoint planes}
\date{2026-11-27}

\p{A field in one coordinate plane can be pulled back to a grid with more directions. When each of several disjoint planes carries its own scalar field, how do their fluxes enter the index of the single Wilson kernel?}

\p{Use the mass-shifted overlap index of \ref{fdip-019X} and the ordered Clifford directions of \ref{fdip-01A1}. Removing a plane will require the inner kernel at three neighboring dimensionless masses.}

